MiniMax-H3 video engine (h3), vendored

Source: the h3 engine repository, branch main, commit 5b55ab7 (ABI v2:
h3_prep, h3_denoise, h3_decode, h3_decode_audio, h3_preview, h3_write_mp4).
A plain copy without its history, by dev/tools/vendor_video.sh:

  h3 runtime/{engine,media,model,ops}/   -> runtime/video/h3/{engine,media,model,ops}/
  h3 runtime/metal/MetalBackend.*        -> runtime/video/h3/metal/
  h3 include/h3/h3.h (C ABI)             -> runtime/video/h3/h3.h
  h3 runtime/metal/abi/                  -> runtime/metal/abi/video/
  h3 runtime/metal/kernels/GROUP/        -> runtime/metal/kernels/video/GROUP/
  h3 tools/convert_*.py, h3/{__init__,common,config,safetensors}.py
                                         -> install/video/

Include paths are rewritten for these places ("engine/" -> "video/h3/engine/"
and likewise for media, metal, model and ops; "metal/abi/" ->
"metal/abi/video/"; "metal/kernels/common/" -> "metal/kernels/video/common/";
"h3/h3.h" -> "video/h3/h3.h"). Code and kernel arithmetic are otherwise
unchanged.

Splash's own files beside the copy: VideoRuntime.* (the engine process of a
video model, which drives the engine through its C ABI), TextEncoder.* and
TextEncoderABI.h with kernels/video/text_encoder.metal (the prompt's text
encoder), and this note.

Build (Makefile): the kernels compile into splash.metallib as its video
group with Splash's production Metal flags, the prep kernels also without
fast math, as h3 builds them, since they reproduce MLX's arithmetic bit for
bit. The host code compiles with Splash's flags plus -ffp-contract=off, as h3
builds it, into build/engine/libsplash-video.a; the mp4 writer links
AVFoundation, CoreMedia and CoreVideo.

Licenses: THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES. No model weights are vendored; the installer
downloads them under the MiniMax H3 Community License Agreement.

